<title>USA: Maine faces $300 mln shortfall in Medicaid program.</title>
<headline>Maine faces $300 mln shortfall in Medicaid program.</headline>
<dateline>AUGUSTA 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maine Gov. Angus King said every option must be considered in developing a plan to close a $300 million short-fall in the state's Medicaid program.</p>
<p>The state must replace lost revenue from the repeal of a controversial tax on hospitals and nursing homes.</p>
<p>The tax money was used to draw hundreds of millions of dollars in federal Medicaid funding to pay for services for the most vulnerable Maine residents, the poor, elderly and disabled people who rely upon the program.</p>
<p>Without the state matching funds the federal contribution will be lost.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
